@@ -547,6 +547,27 @@
    `key`, `lock` and `condition` parameters are also available as
    :attr:`cache`, :attr:`cache_key`, :attr:`cache_lock` and
    :attr:`cache_condition` attributes of the wrapped instance method.
+   Note that, as with :attr:`cache`, :attr:`cache_lock` and
+   :attr:`cache_condition`, the :attr:`cache_key` attribute is bound to
+   the instance, i.e. the instance's ``self`` argument is passed
+   implicitly, so `obj.method.cache_key(*args, **kwargs)` returns the
+   key used for caching `obj.method(*args, **kwargs)`:
+
+   .. testcode::
+
+      class CachedNumbers:
+
+          def __init__(self):
+              self.cache = LRUCache(maxsize=32)
+
+          @cachedmethod(lambda self: self.cache)
+          def square(self, n):
+              return n * n
+
+      numbers = CachedNumbers()
+      numbers.square(42)
+      numbers.square.cache.pop(numbers.square.cache_key(42), None)
+
    A :func:`cache_clear()` function will also be provided, as well as
    an optional :func:`cache_info()` function reporting per-instance
    cache statistics.
